From c3e4143157e424d6d2cfe372e1ece3bfff4a7b21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:20:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Support arbitrary UART baud rates

The baud rate for the server tty ("baud") and the local tty
("local-tty-baud"), as well as the D-Bus Baud property, were limited to
the standard termios Bxxx rates. Some hosts use non-standard rates such
as 134400, which could not be configured.

Store baud rates as plain integers and program the tty through the
Linux termios2 interface (TCGETS2/TCSETS2 with BOTHER), which accepts
any rate the UART driver can approximate. Standard rates keep working
unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
